+ *
+ * Three ways to get the pixels out (PAN_WGL_PRESENT picks one; their cost is
+ * logged every PRESENT_CYCLE frames to C:\mali\log\<exe>-<pid>-gl.txt).
+ * Measured on the Pixel 6 (2026-11-19, ms per present at 621x480 and
+ * 617x1371): 0 = 8.6 / 9.9-19, 1 = 5.9 / 12.7, 2 = 6.5 / 12.3. Reading
+ * write-combined memory (~400 MB/s) is most of it; 1 is the default.
+ *  0  map the colour buffer itself: the map waits for the frame and
+ *     resolves Panfrost's tiled or AFBC layout on the CPU
+ *  1  a GPU blit into a linear B8G8R8A8 staging texture, mapped and handed
+ *     to StretchDIBits as it is (GDI reads write-combined memory)
+ *  2  the same, copied once into cached memory before GDI reads it
